714:
Sexually oriented businesses shall not be located in any zoning district other than as provided by chapter 98, Zoning, of this Code.
(1) No sexually oriented business shall be operated within:
a. 1,000 feet of a church, synagogue or other place used regularly for religious worship;
b. 1,000 feet of a public or private school;
c. 1,000 feet of a boundary of any residential district;
d. 1,000 feet of a historic district;
e. 1,000 feet of a medical facility;
f. 1,000 feet of any building occupied by any department or agency of any government;
g. 1,000 feet of an establishment licensed to sell alcoholic beverages;
h. 1,000 feet of a publicly owned recreational facility or public park;
i. 1,000 feet of a licensed day-care center;
j. 1,000 feet of an entertainment business that is oriented primarily towards children or family entertainment; or
k. 1,000 feet of another sexually oriented business.
(2) A sexually oriented business may not be operated in the same building, structure, or portion thereof, containing another sexually oriented business classified pursuant to section 68-3.
(3) For the purposes of this chapter, measurement shall be made in a straight line, without regard to intervening structures or objects, from the nearest portion of the building or structure used as a part of the premises where a sexually oriented business is conducted, to the nearest property line of any of the premises described in subsection (1) of this section.
(Ord. No. 909, § 1, 4-4-00)

